{"id": "EUVD-2026-64416", "enisaUuid": "9d498fad-b511-3894-8195-b0d0ab1b5e48", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsoc: aspeed: lpc-snoop: Fix usercopy overflow in snoop_file_read\n\nput_fifo_with_discard() acts as both producer and consumer on the kfifo:\nit calls kfifo_skip() (advances out) and kfifo_put() (advances in) from\nthe IRQ handler without synchronizing with snoop_file_read(), which also\nconsumes via kfifo_to_user(). On SMP systems this concurrent access can\nleave (in - out) larger than the ring buffer, so __kfifo_to_user()'s clamp\nto (in - out) is ineffective and kfifo_copy_to_user() can attempt a\ncopy_to_user() past the kmalloc-2k backing store:\n\n  usercopy: Kernel memory exposure attempt detected from SLUB object\n  'kmalloc-2k' (offset 0, size 2049)!\n  kernel BUG at mm/usercopy.c!\n  Call trace:\n   usercopy_abort\n   __check_heap_object\n   __check_object_size\n   kfifo_copy_to_user\n   __kfifo_to_user\n   snoop_file_read\n   vfs_read\n\nSerialize kfifo access with a per-channel spinlock shared between the\nIRQ handler (producer) and the file reader (consumer).  Annotate @fifo\nwith __guarded_by(&lock) and opt the driver into context analysis so the\ncompiler enforces that all fifo access holds the lock.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:33:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b87c0d24386ed5106feac12034fe09d893ccb469", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/afe2527eae0b51d5e8ddd77293afab3a5a1311a4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/868c478abce858135db3eb65548a577e4b6747ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/131ab677b03349a5ae48da8722ec7075b37ec66e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1acef6d85bfd98bd9dfe1f08bffa397a4dda8a6f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6hj9-w6w6-x26p", "CVE-2026-74729"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0821b9aa-a032-33e2-9a14-285d479cdbea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19"}, {"id": "3200a74c-a496-3f7f-a531-1496dbd2ba30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "575e76a5-3547-3929-94df-5f060fb37a26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "5acab37f-7a3f-3f7c-9395-7636b17468bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3772e5da445420543b25825ac2b5971f3743f6e8 <b87c0d24386ed5106feac12034fe09d893ccb469"}, {"id": "63abf3ab-8ce7-3ba9-8e0f-9daae18cc593", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8055994a-d920-300a-bdfb-7fc38a6821f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "90c88482-4d24-3bf4-a0ed-63c73376a373", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3772e5da445420543b25825ac2b5971f3743f6e8 <131ab677b03349a5ae48da8722ec7075b37ec66e"}, {"id": "a49aa8ea-e5e0-34d5-a7ca-ffa251dc1fa9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3772e5da445420543b25825ac2b5971f3743f6e8 <1acef6d85bfd98bd9dfe1f08bffa397a4dda8a6f"}, {"id": "a97304c1-4f6a-3d9c-a3b3-60c18a8abd9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "ca5cf524-3ed6-33b3-aaff-ade34aa7ca21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "de7dc59b-9014-38b2-adb6-b9f344447171", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3772e5da445420543b25825ac2b5971f3743f6e8 <868c478abce858135db3eb65548a577e4b6747ac"}, {"id": "f7b6feb4-784a-3e58-b289-8d0524333f8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3772e5da445420543b25825ac2b5971f3743f6e8 <afe2527eae0b51d5e8ddd77293afab3a5a1311a4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c076adc7-fd3d-3a8f-bd31-e